course: dictionary
lesson: 10103
title: Think: many meanings, one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word think has more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. They are its context, and they give you clues. «Toad thinks a long time and then says sadly...» Toad is not sitting still, he is working something out in his head.
explain: «I think it will rain» means you believe it or have an opinion. You cannot see the rain yet, so this is what you believe. «Think of a name for your puppy» means make up an idea. Here you are inventing something, not remembering it.
explain: Think can also mean remember. «Think back to your last birthday» means bring it into your mind. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Think is a verb. Its forms are think, thinks, thought and thinking. Thought is also a noun.
fact: To think is to use your mind to work something out.
fact: To think something is to believe it or have an opinion: «I think it will rain».
fact: To think of or about something is to have it in your mind or to remember it, as in «think back».
fact: Common phrases with think: «think about», «think of», «think so», «think twice» and «think ahead».
exercise: «Toad thinks a long time and then says sadly...» What does thinks mean here? | *To use your mind to work something out | To buy something new | To sleep soundly | To run away quickly
exercise: «I think it will rain.» What does think mean here? | To count the clouds | *To believe it or have an opinion | To measure the rain | To shout loudly
exercise: Which word is a noun as well as a form of think? | think | *thought | thinking | thinks
test: «Think of a name for the new puppy.» What does think of mean here? | *To make up an idea | To lose something | To eat slowly | To sing a song
test: Which phrase means to plan for the future? | think about | think of | think so | *think ahead
exam: «Think back to your last birthday party.» What does think back mean here? | To run very fast | To paint a picture | *To remember | To jump high
